1
00:00:00,730 --> 00:00:07,030
What if I told you a Ghana Premier League
club kept 24 clean sheets in 34 matches...

2
00:00:07,570 --> 00:00:09,670
and still didn't win the title?

3
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:20,270
In the 2025/26 season, Hearts of Oak
conceded just 15 goals throughout the
entire league campaign.

4
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:23,690
They kept an incredible 24 clean sheets.

5
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:27,110
But here's the surprising part.

6
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:31,890
13 of those clean sheets ended in goalless
draws.

7
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:35,930
Thirteen matches where their opponents
couldn't score...

8
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:37,910
but neither could Hearts.

9
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,430
And that's the problem.

10
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,630
Football isn't just about stopping goals.

11
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:45,930
You also have to score them.

12
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:50,450
Hearts managed only 25 goals in 34
matches.

13
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:57,530
That's an average of just 0.74 goals per
game, compared to the league average of
1.02.

14
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:02,650
In fact, they failed to score in 18
matches.

15
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:07,150
Now, compare that with the eventual
champions, Medeama.

16
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:10,630
Both clubs lost exactly six matches.

17
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:16,710
But while Medeama won 17 games, Hearts
managed just 13.

18
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:23,890
And that difference in wins and draws left
Hearts eight points behind the champions.

19
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:27,670
Hearts had an extraordinary defence.

20
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:32,070
But they couldn't turn enough of those
clean sheets into victories.

21
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,910
Unpacked by GilB.

22
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,230
There's more to the story.
